  "findings": [
    {"id":"integer-turn-boundaries","status":"verified_fix","sites":["0x000A3059","0x000895B8","0x0010E4FB"],"cases":["goal-flight"],"evidence":"Shared integer increment now uses the actual previous phase. Original goal-flight path and independent quaternion rule reproduce the rounding failure at 75/1000 Hz and irregular intervals; other users share the helper but retain their own gameplay coverage obligations."},
    {"id":"world-countdown","status":"verified_fix","sites":["0x000A80E2","0x000A80E3"],"cases":["world-countdown"],"evidence":"Positive signed WORLD+1C duration is a rule counter. Only its decrement is gated; traversal, responses and matrix construction remain per scene."},
    {"id":"world-replay-response","status":"verified_fix","sites":["0x000A7DE8","0x000A7E11","0x000A7E15","0x000A7E1A","0x000A7EB6","0x000A7EE1","0x000A7EE5","0x000A7EEA"],"cases":["world-replay-relaxation","world-replay-target"],"evidence":"The original /4 response acts on signed angles. Fractional exponential response carries angle precision in the four verified WORLD records; both controllers are checked against independent formulas and original 60 Hz bytes."},
    {"id":"world-existing-relaxation","status":"verified_fix","sites":["0x000A7D45","0x000A7D48","0x000A78C9","0x000A7AFD","0x000A7820"],"cases":["world-existing-relaxation","world-individual-reset"],"evidence":"Previous scaling at A7D1B/A7D2E still rounded signed tilt after every small step, losing up to 25.8 angle units in five ticks at 1000 Hz. Carry precision at the final store and invalidate it on original per-record initialization or transition to the vector/scripted controller; retain original full-tick bytes."},
    {"id":"world-steering-response","status":"verified_fix","sites":["0x000A7F94","0x000A7FC1","0x000A8000"],"cases":["world-steering-neutral","world-steering-input","world-steering-clamped","world-steering-paused","world-steering-pause-resume","world-steering-reset"],"evidence":"Compose original .2 response and .8 decay before fractional iteration. Preserve original full-tick conversions; reset fractional history at the original four-record initializer. Numeric scope covers neutral/clamped input, opposite signs, pause and reset."},
    {"id":"ball-size-expiry","status":"verified_fix","sites":["0x0008BC7C","0x0008BC90","0x0008BCA7","0x0008BCD1"],"cases":["ball-size","ball-size-expiration"],"evidence":"Use only the active part of an interval for shrinking; original expiry tick holds radius, then the trailing phase begins recovery. Every sample through expiry is checked."},
    {"id":"info-initialization","status":"not_time_dependent","sites":["0x00013C43"],"cases":[],"evidence":"13B70 is the INFO initializer, reached via the event lifecycle. Its conditional 6C7D2C increment accompanies course initialization, not elapsed scene time. Bounded original analysis: timing/research/original/0x00013B70.json."},
    {"id":"draw-depth-offset","status":"not_time_dependent","sites":["0x0001F4D3"],"cases":[],"evidence":"1F4C0 adjusts current draw-context +F8. 5A5A0 calls it with +0.5, draws the queue, then calls -0.5: a scoped drawing offset, not a velocity. Leave the original arithmetic intact."},
    {"id":"draw-queue-allocation","status":"not_time_dependent","sites":["0x0001F53C","0x0001F642","0x0001F724","0x0001F784","0x0001F80F","0x0001F815"],"cases":[],"evidence":"1F4E0/1F570/1F660 clamp the computed draw depth bucket to count minus one. At 531AA..531CB the caller computes the bucket, reserves 0x14 bytes via 1F7E0 and inserts the packet via 1F770, which increments the draw-context count. 1F820 clears the list/count and restores the arena cursor and free bytes. None of these fields measure elapsed time."},
    {"id":"storage-dialog-fade","status":"verified_fix","sites":["0x0001DD6D","0x0001DD6E","0x0001DD86","0x0001DD8A","0x0001DD9F","0x0001DDA1"],"cases":["dialog-opening","dialog-closing","dialog-clamped"],"evidence":"1DD10 mixes recurring drawing with 6D010C duration clamped to 0..8; alpha is count*0.1 at 1DDA5. Advance duration on rule ticks and sample alpha per scene, including the first opening fraction. Prefix probes stop explicitly at 74F10, before drawing; original 60 Hz counter and alpha bytes are pinned."},
    {"id":"animation-blend-clock","status":"verified_fix","sites":["0x00097E0C","0x00097E13","0x00097E1C","0x0009C5B5","0x0009AEE0"],"cases":["animation-blend-in-progress","animation-blend-completion","animation-blend-clip-selection"],"evidence":"97E00 advances the elapsed clock on rule ticks and samples its original pre-increment weight per scene. At expiry the secondary clip flag and both clocks clear on the original tick. 9C540 and 9AED0 use the same active interval when selecting a clip or querying completion. Prefix probes pin weights, clock/flag bytes and the pending-clip branch; the CPU diagnostic checks the query."},
    {"id":"animation-playhead-boundaries","status":"verified_fix","sites":["0x00097D28","0x00097D46","0x00097D80","0x00097DAD","0x00097DC1","0x00097DD9","0x00097DDE","0x00097DFA","0x00098B62","0x00098B71","0x00099319","0x0009932B","0x00099385","0x0009938F","0x0009AEC3","0x0009C59E"],"cases":["animation-clock","animation-forward-wrap","animation-reverse-wrap","animation-one-shot-completion","animation-fractional-speed-wrap"],"evidence":"97D20 keeps its full rule-tick increment for both bounds and wrap distance. 99300 samples the phase once per clip before its 98B50 bone loop. At high refresh the same pre-advance interval survives into intermediate scenes; loop counters and completion stay on the original rule. Prefix probes cover both pose inputs, forward and reverse restart, and one-shot hold. CPU diagnostics separately exercise the end queries."},
    {"id":"animation-playhead-lifecycle","status":"verified_fix","sites":["0x00098962","0x0009ADED"],"cases":["animation-same-time-seek","animation-secondary-copy"],"evidence":"9ADE0 is an explicit seek even when the requested float equals the advanced playhead. It invalidates the prior sample. 98920 copies the outgoing track to the secondary blend slot and transfers its pose interval before 978E0 initializes the new primary track."},
    {"id":"character-cue-clocks","status":"verified_fix","sites":["0x0009CBF0","0x0009CE60","0x0009CE99","0x0009D01A","0x000954FE","0x00095792","0x000957CC","0x0009590A"],"cases":["character-cue-clock","menu-character-cue-clock"],"evidence":"9C540 and 94F60 mix pose work with original PRNG rolls, cue state transitions and duration updates. Keep each cue's rolls, transitions, increments and decrements on rule ticks. Resume through the original saved-register cleanup and 98B20 model call. Captured-model prefixes check seed, cue start, expiry, misses and model argument across the schedule matrix."},
    {"id":"character-blend-rate-limit","status":"verified_fix","sites":["0x0009541D","0x00095436","0x00095440","0x000954B7","0x000954D0","0x000954DA","0x000956B4","0x000956CD","0x000956D7","0x0009574D","0x00095766","0x00095770","0x0009CB1C","0x0009CB35","0x0009CB3F","0x0009CBA3","0x0009CBBC","0x0009CBC6","0x0009CD94","0x0009CDAD","0x0009CDB7","0x0009CE1B","0x0009CE34","0x0009CE3E"],"cases":["character-blend-rate-limit","menu-character-blend-rate-limit"],"evidence":"The original comparison and the signed step both use the three-unit 347B84 constant. Scale both by the scene interval in the menu and actor paths, so the target is reached at the same elapsed time. Captured-model prefixes cover both signs, intermediate samples and exact endpoint bytes."},
    {"id":"text-box-reveal-and-scale","status":"verified_fix","sites":["0x0006BC95","0x0006BC96","0x0006BCB6","0x0006BBB3","0x0006BBF8"],"cases":["text-box-reveal","text-box-pause-resume","text-box-closing"],"evidence":"6BB60 advances its reveal clock and dispatches 6B8F0 once per original rule tick after the delay. The 0.1 and 0.15 scale and appearance gains compose across rendered scenes. Full calls with a real glyph queue check the original reveal ticks, cursor, terminator, pause and both scale paths."},
    {"id":"text-glyph-bookkeeping","status":"not_time_dependent","sites":["0x0006ACA7","0x0006B964","0x0006B980","0x0006BA09","0x0006BA3A","0x0006BA63"],"cases":[],"evidence":"6AC40 clamps a parsed style index. 6B8F0 moves its ring indices, line number and width per parsed token. 6A850 counts glyphs before a delay escape; 6BA3A transitions the delay over those glyphs. The reveal caller owns elapsed time and these per-token operations retain their original arithmetic."},
    {"id":"text-box-anchor-and-roll","status":"verified_fix","sites":["0x0006BB60","0x0006B520","0x0006BBC2","0x0006BC60","0x0006BC91","0x0006BCCC","0x0006BE2F","0x0006C1FA","0x0006C2B7"],"cases":["text-box-roll","text-box-anchored-placement"],"evidence":"The verified 6BB60 rule advances placement and the signed angular spring together. Fractional scenes evaluate the original placement against a private text-box copy, then sample that result for 6B520 drawing. The guest pose and the old relative vector used by the next rule are unchanged by drawing. Probes preserve detached pause/resume and captured anchored placement, velocity and roll through four original ticks."}
